      "finding": "For FY2017 the two sources disagree by a factor of 2.13: SEC EDGAR holds 769,300,000 and Alpha Vantage holds 1,636,000,000. This is a difference of SCOPE, not a correction. Tesla used the DepreciationDepletionAndAmortization tag in only one filing, the FY2017 Form 10-K, and tagged a narrower figure with it; the tag does not appear for FY2018 or FY2019 at all. Alpha Vantage's series is the total depreciation, amortisation and impairment line, and its FY2016 value of 947,099,000 matches Tesla's reported total for that year.",
      "which_is_used": "Alpha Vantage, because it is the only source that covers all three years on one basis, because its two statements corroborate each other, and because the resulting EBITDA reconciles with Tesla's reported FY2019 adjusted EBITDA once stock-based compensation is added back. The EDGAR value is NOT used and is recorded here so the disagreement stays visible.",
      "unresolved": "What the narrower EDGAR figure covers is not established. Settling it needs the FY2017 filing's own tagging, and data.sec.gov is denied by this environment's network policy."
